<section>
		<section>
			<h1>Logical reading order</h1>
		</section>

		<section id="ordre">	
			
			<ul>
			<li>Put source code in logical order</li>
			<li>Logical order generally corresponds to reading order</li>
			<li>Don't cut logical blocks in two</li>
		</ul>

		</section>
					
		<section>
            <h2>Example: reading order incorrect</h2>
            <img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/structure/couleurs.png" alt="Blue square wit its 5 color codes (RGB, CMJN, RVB, etc)">
           <p>In source code: 'PMS, CMJN, RVB, HEXA, RAL, Blue 072 C, 100 85 0 5 , 47 62 139, #2F3E8B, 5022'.</p>
       </section>

       <section>
       	<h2>Don't put content before its heading in source code</h2>

       	<p><img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/structure/card_finshop.png" alt="Card on finshop website with heading at bottom of card"><img src="https://images.anysurfer.be/structure/card_bbcnews.png" alt="Card on BBC news website with heading at the top of card"></p>

       </section>


		<section>
			<h2>Example: different visual order and reading order</h2>
			<pre><code is:raw>&lt;ul id="menu"&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#"&gt;4 Contact&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#"&gt;3 Blog&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#"&gt;2 About us&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
 &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="#"&gt;1 Home&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt; 
&lt;/ul&gt; </code></pre>
<pre><code is:raw>#menu li { 
float: right; 
